{
  "title": "Private Fields and Getters",
  "summary": "Real privacy with #fields, TypeScript's private, and get/set accessors.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Two kinds of private",
      "body": [
        "```ts",
        "class Account {",
        "  #balance = 0;              // JavaScript private field: enforced at run time",
        "  private audit: string[] = [];   // TypeScript private: checked by tsc only, erased",
        "",
        "  deposit(n: number) {",
        "    this.#balance += n;",
        "    this.audit.push(`+${n}`);",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "",
        "const a = new Account();",
        "a.#balance;      // SyntaxError: the language itself forbids it, even in plain JS",
        "a.audit;         // tsc error, but the property is really there at run time",
        "```",
        "",
        "Prefer `#fields` for real encapsulation. They are invisible to `JSON.stringify`, `Object.keys` and spread, which is usually what you want for internal state. `private` (and `protected`, `readonly`) are compile-time checks, like many C# access modifiers would be if reflection did not exist."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "class Box {",
        "  #secret = 42;",
        "  label = \"box\";",
        "  reveal() { return this.#secret; }",
        "}",
        "const b = new Box();",
        "console.log(JSON.stringify(b), Object.keys(b).length, b.reveal());"
      ],
      "answer": "{\"label\":\"box\"} 1 42",
      "explain": "`#secret` is not a normal property: it does not show up in JSON or `Object.keys`, but methods of the class can read it."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Getters and setters",
      "body": [
        "`get` and `set` define properties backed by code, like C# properties:",
        "",
        "```ts",
        "class Temperature {",
        "  #celsius = 0;",
        "",
        "  get celsius() { return this.#celsius; }",
        "  set celsius(v: number) {",
        "    if (v < -273.15) throw new RangeError(\"below absolute zero\");",
        "    this.#celsius = v;",
        "  }",
        "",
        "  get fahrenheit() { return this.#celsius * 9 / 5 + 32; }   // read-only: no setter",
        "}",
        "",
        "const t = new Temperature();",
        "t.celsius = 25;          // runs the setter",
        "t.fahrenheit;            // 77, no parentheses",
        "```",
        "",
        "A getter with no setter is read-only. Assigning to it is a `tsc` error; at run time it throws a `TypeError` in strict-mode code (ES modules and class bodies) and is silently ignored in old-style scripts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "class Cart {",
        "  #items: number[] = [];",
        "  add(price: number) { this.#items.push(price); return this; }",
        "  get count() { return this.#items.length; }",
        "  get total() { return this.#items.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0); }",
        "}",
        "const c = new Cart().add(3).add(4);",
        "console.log(c.count, c.total);",
        "(c as any).count = 10;",
        "console.log(c.count);"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "2 7",
        "2"
      ],
      "explain": "Getters are read like fields. A getter without a setter cannot be assigned: in this file the assignment is silently ignored, and in strict-mode code (ES modules, class bodies) it throws a `TypeError`. Either way `count` stays 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "prompt": "Enforced when the program runs, or only by `tsc`?",
      "buckets": [
        "enforced at run time",
        "only checked by tsc"
      ],
      "items": [
        [
          "`#count` field",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`private count`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`readonly id`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "a getter with no setter (in a class)",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`protected` method",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`Object.freeze(this)`",
          0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Complete the class so `name` is validated and `initials` is read-only.",
      "code": [
        "class Person {",
        "  __1__name = \"\";",
        "  __2__ name() { return this.#name; }",
        "  __3__ name(v: string) {",
        "    if (!v.trim()) throw new Error(\"name required\");",
        "    this.#name = v.trim();",
        "  }",
        "  get initials() { return this.#name.split(\" \").map(p => p[0]).join(\"\"); }",
        "}"
      ],
      "blanks": [
        "#",
        "get",
        "set"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "private ",
        "set",
        "get"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "A stack with private storage",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `class Stack<T>` with a private `#items: T[]` and:",
        "",
        "- `push(x: T): void`",
        "- `pop(): T | undefined`",
        "- `peek(): T | undefined` (top item, not removed)",
        "- a getter `size`",
        "- a getter `isEmpty`",
        "",
        "`JSON.stringify(new Stack())` must be `\"{}\"` (nothing public leaks)."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "class Stack<T> {",
        "  // your code",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "class Stack<T> {",
        "  #items: T[] = [];",
        "  push(x: T): void {",
        "    this.#items.push(x);",
        "  }",
        "  pop(): T | undefined {",
        "    return this.#items.pop();",
        "  }",
        "  peek(): T | undefined {",
        "    return this.#items[this.#items.length - 1];",
        "  }",
        "  get size() {",
        "    return this.#items.length;",
        "  }",
        "  get isEmpty() {",
        "    return this.#items.length === 0;",
        "  }",
        "}"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "const dojoS = new Stack<string>();",
        "Dojo.eq(\"new stack isEmpty\", true, dojoS.isEmpty);",
        "dojoS.push(\"a\"); dojoS.push(\"b\");",
        "Dojo.eq(\"size after two pushes\", 2, dojoS.size);",
        "Dojo.eq(\"peek()\", \"b\", dojoS.peek());",
        "Dojo.eq(\"pop()\", \"b\", dojoS.pop());",
        "Dojo.eq(\"size after pop\", 1, dojoS.size);",
        "Dojo.eq(\"pop() on empty gives undefined\", true, (dojoS.pop(), dojoS.pop()) === undefined);",
        "Dojo.eq(\"nothing public leaks\", \"{}\", JSON.stringify(new Stack<number>()));"
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "#items",
          "message": "Uses a #private field"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "get\\s+size",
          "message": "size is a getter"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`#items: T[] = [];`",
        "`get size() { return this.#items.length; }`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Validated settings",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `class Volume` holding a private level from 0 to 100 (starts at 50):",
        "",
        "- getter/setter `level`: the setter **clamps** to 0 to 100 and rounds to an integer",
        "- getter `muted`: `true` when the level is 0",
        "- method `toggleMute()`: when not muted, remembers the level and sets 0; when muted, restores the remembered level (or 50 if nothing was remembered)"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "class Volume {",
        "  // your code",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "class Volume {",
        "  #level = 50;",
        "  #saved: number | null = null;",
        "  get level() {",
        "    return this.#level;",
        "  }",
        "  set level(v: number) {",
        "    this.#level = Math.round(Math.min(100, Math.max(0, v)));",
        "  }",
        "  get muted() {",
        "    return this.#level === 0;",
        "  }",
        "  toggleMute() {",
        "    if (this.muted) {",
        "      this.#level = this.#saved ?? 50;",
        "      this.#saved = null;",
        "    } else {",
        "      this.#saved = this.#level;",
        "      this.#level = 0;",
        "    }",
        "  }",
        "}"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "const dojoV = new Volume();",
        "Dojo.eq(\"starts at 50\", 50, dojoV.level);",
        "dojoV.level = 140;",
        "Dojo.eq(\"clamps to 100\", 100, dojoV.level);",
        "dojoV.level = 33.6;",
        "Dojo.eq(\"rounds\", 34, dojoV.level);",
        "dojoV.toggleMute();",
        "Dojo.eq(\"muted\", true, dojoV.muted);",
        "dojoV.toggleMute();",
        "Dojo.eq(\"restores level\", 34, dojoV.level);",
        "const dojoV2 = new Volume();",
        "dojoV2.level = -5;",
        "dojoV2.toggleMute();",
        "Dojo.eq(\"unmuting from 0 with nothing saved gives 50\", 50, dojoV2.level);"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Keep `#level` and `#saved`.",
        "Clamp with `Math.min(100, Math.max(0, v))` then `Math.round`."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
